# Quick View Product Modal - Complete Production-Ready Solution

## File 1: README.md

```markdown
# Quick View Product Modal

A production-ready Shopify snippet that enables customers to preview product details, select variants, and add to cart directly from collection pages without navigating away.

## What It Solves

- **Reduces friction**: Customers can quickly view product details without leaving the collection page
- **Increases conversions**: Add-to-cart functionality directly in the modal reduces steps to purchase
- **Improves UX**: Variant selection, image gallery, and full product info in an accessible overlay
- **Maintains context**: Customers don't lose their place while browsing collections

## Features

- ✅ Full variant selection with dynamic price updates
- ✅ Image gallery with thumbnail navigation
- ✅ Add to cart with AJAX (no page reload)
- ✅ Quantity selector
- ✅ Stock availability display
- ✅ Mobile-responsive design
- ✅ Full keyboard navigation (Tab, Escape, Arrow keys)
- ✅ WCAG 2.1 AA accessible (ARIA labels, focus management, screen reader support)
- ✅ Works with OS 2.0 themes (Dawn, Horizon, Craft)
- ✅ No external dependencies
- ✅ Lazy-loaded product data for performance

## Installation

### Step 1: Add the Snippet File

Copy `quick-view-modal-product.liquid` to your theme's `snippets/` folder.

### Step 2: Add the JavaScript File

Copy `snippet.js` contents and either:

**Option A**: Add to your theme's `assets/` folder as `quick-view-modal.js` and include in `theme.liquid`:
```liquid
<script src="{{ 'quick-view-modal.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
```

**Option B**: Include inline in `theme.liquid` before `</body>`:
```liquid
<script>
  // Paste snippet.js contents here
</script>
```

### Step 3: Add Modal Container to Theme

Add this line to `layout/theme.liquid` just before `</body>`:
```liquid
{% render 'quick-view-modal-product' %}
```

### Step 4: Add Quick View Buttons to Product Cards

In your product card snippet (usually `snippets/card-product.liquid` or `snippets/product-card.liquid`), add:

```liquid
{% render 'quick-view-modal-product',
  trigger_only: true,
  product: product,
  button_style: 'primary'
%}
```

## Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
|-----------|------|---------|-------------|
| `trigger_only` | Boolean | `false` | When `true`, only renders the trigger button (use in product cards) |
| `product` | Product | `nil` | Product object (required when `trigger_only: true`) |
| `button_style` | String | `'primary'` | Button style: `'primary'`, `'secondary'`, `'minimal'`, `'icon-only'` |
| `button_text` | String | `'Quick View'` | Custom button text |
| `show_vendor` | Boolean | `true` | Show product vendor in modal |
| `show_sku` | Boolean | `false` | Show variant SKU in modal |
| `show_share` | Boolean | `true` | Show social share buttons |
| `enable_video` | Boolean | `true` | Enable video media in gallery |
| `image_size` | String | `'large'` | Main image size: `'small'`, `'medium'`, `'large'` |
| `max_thumbnails` | Number | `5` | Maximum thumbnails to display |

## Example Usage

### Basic Implementation (Collection Page)

```liquid
{% for product in collection.products %}
  <div class="product-card">
    <a href="{{ product.url }}">
      <img src="{{ product.featured_image | img_url: '400x' }}" alt="{{ product.title }}">
      <h3>{{ product.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ product.price | money }}</p>
    </a>
    
    {% render 'quick-view-modal-product',
      trigger_only: true,
      product: product
    %}
  </div>
{% endfor %}
```

### Icon-Only Button

```liquid
{% render 'quick-view-modal-product',
  trigger_only: true,
  product: product,
  button_style: 'icon-only'
%}
```

### Custom Styled Button

```liquid
{% render 'quick-view-modal-product',
  trigger_only: true,
  product: product,
  button_style: 'secondary',
  button_text: 'Preview'
%}
```

### Full Modal with Custom Options

```liquid
{% render 'quick-view-modal-product',
  show_vendor: false,
  show_sku: true,
  show_share: false,
  max_thumbnails: 8
%}
```

## Customization

### CSS Custom Properties

Override these CSS variables in your theme's stylesheet:

```css
:root {
  --qv-modal-bg: #ffffff;
  --qv-overlay-bg: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
  --qv-primary-color: #000000;
  --qv-secondary-color: #666666;
  --qv-border-color: #e5e5e5;
  --qv-button-bg: #000000;
  --qv-button-text: #ffffff;
  --qv-button-hover-bg: #333333;
  --qv-error-color: #dc3545;
  --qv-success-color: #28a745;
  --qv-font-family: inherit;
  --qv-border-radius: 8px;
  --qv-transition-speed: 0.3s;
}
```

### Events

The modal dispatches custom events you can listen for:

```javascript
// Modal opened
document.addEventListener('quickview:opened', (e) => {
  console.log('Quick view opened for:', e.detail.productId);
});

// Modal closed
document.addEventListener('quickview:closed', () => {
  console.log('Quick view closed');
});

// Product added to cart
document.addEventListener('quickview:added', (e) => {
  console.log('Added to cart:', e.detail);
});

// Variant changed
document.addEventListener('quickview:variant-changed', (e) => {
  console.log('Variant changed:', e.detail.variant);
});
```

## Browser Support

- Chrome 60+
- Firefox 55+
- Safari 12+
- Edge 79+
- iOS Safari 12+
- Chrome for Android 60+

## Troubleshooting

### Modal not opening
1. Ensure the modal container is added to `theme.liquid`
2. Check browser console for JavaScript errors
3. Verify product handle is being passed correctly

### Styles conflicting with theme
1. Increase CSS specificity by wrapping in additional class
2. Check for `!important` declarations in theme CSS
3. Adjust CSS custom properties to match theme

### Add to cart not working
1. Verify your theme's cart API endpoint (`/cart/add.js`)
2. Check if theme uses custom cart functionality
3. Look for CORS or CSP errors in console

## Performance Notes

- Product data is fetched via AJAX only when modal opens (lazy loading)
- Images use native lazy loading
- Modal DOM is reused for all products (single instance)
- CSS is scoped and doesn't affect theme styles

